// board.mn — the medium's standing verdict on its own source.
//
// A BOARD LINE is a named invariant of the wheel, the bound it may not cross,
// and the SITES the medium finds for it live. Every line's sites are the
// answer to a `mentl query` question — the same `ask` the verb renders — so
// the board asks the medium a question the medium already answers, and
// nothing between the two re-derives it. The count is `len` of that list and
// is never stored beside it.
//
// WHAT THIS REPLACES, and why the replacement is the point rather than the
// tidying. The bounds lived in `tools/verify-baseline.txt`: 1,695 lines
// holding 26 numbers, 1,669 of them prose justifying those numbers. Each
// check ran the medium, RENDERED the count to a sentence, re-parsed the
// sentence with a regex, and compared the result against a number grepped
// out of that file. Three re-derivations of one fact — the count the walk
// had already computed, the bound the project had already decided, and the
// verdict a shell `if` then invented. The prose was the deepest loss: a
// bound's justification is a Reason, and a Reason belongs on the node it
// justifies, so each bound below carries its own — walkable by `mentl why`,
// rendered as its `Lede:` at its own address, and impossible to separate
// from the number it explains.
//
// WHAT A BOUND IS NOT. A bound is not a proof. Fourteen of the old file's
// keys read ZERO, and a ratchet held at zero is a proxy for a proof nobody
// minted (PLAN §7, in those words). The ultimate form of every line here is
// its own DELETION: the shape becomes a `DiagKind` the executable refuses,
// `diag_refuses` holds the invariant directly, and the line retires the way
// the use-after-move ratchet did at pin 21696779. So this roster is a COUNTDOWN,
// and a line that never falls is not a passing gate — it is 8.4's universal
// executable refusal, unbuilt, saying so.
import types

import query

// One measured invariant: the QUESTION the medium answers by place and the
// count of sites it may not exceed. The two fields are inseparable — a
// question with no bound is a report, and a bound with no question is the
// text file this replaces.
//
// A QUESTION, NOT A SHAPE (G2). The board bounded census shapes alone, so
// what the medium answers any other way rose with nothing to refuse it: the
// open proof obligations went 37 → 39 across one landing, read by a facet
// (`smt`) and bounded by nobody. Every `mentl query` question whose answer
// is a list of sites — a census shape, a prose class, the open obligations,
// the ghosts — is a line here, and a question answered without sites
// refuses as a bound rather than counting nothing (`located_answer`).
type Bound = {ceiling: Int, question: Question}

// What the medium found when it looked: the SITES, not a count of them.
//
// This arm carried an `Int` for one day and the Int was a COPY — `census_sites`
// returns the located list and the count is `len` of it, so storing the number
// beside the list it came from is the Carried-Truth violation this module was
// written to end, committed inside the module that ends it. The list rides both
// arms because a board that only speaks when it fails cannot show a countdown
// moving, and the falling number is the whole reason these lines exist.
//
// It is also what lets a breach say WHICH — a bound that reports "367, was 365"
// tells the developer a number rose; a bound that names its sites tells them
// where to look, from a list the walk already built and the verb used to throw
// away.
//
// The label rides beside the sites because the board asks the medium's own
// question and renders the medium's own answer: the label is part of what
// `located_answer` handed back, never a second spelling kept here. A bound
// whose question the medium answers without sites is UNLOCATED — the
// roster's mistake, which refuses like a breach instead of passing on zero.
type Standing = Within(String, [(String, Span)]) | Over(String, [(String, Span)]) | Unlocated(String)

// The roster, complete by construction: a shape absent here is not measured,
// which is visible, where a shape measured against a missing bound would be
// a silent pass. Each entry's prose is its justification — the `why` the old
// file kept 1,669 lines away from the number it belonged to.
fn board_bounds() = [
  // Zero because an eta-wrapper is a REFERENCE written as a MINT: the name it
  // wraps already exists, so the lambda re-mints what a handle would have
  // carried. A NAMED forwarder is not counted here: the surface wants some
  // (`fanout`, `delay`, `len` — vocabulary and typed faces, `census_matches`
  // carries the measurement), so a count of them could not hold at zero
  // without claiming the language is wrong. Retires when the shape is a
  // refusal rather than a count.
  Bound({ceiling: 0, question: QCensus(CsEta)}),
  // The one line here that is a COUNTDOWN rather than a held zero: a
  // REFERENCE WRITTEN AS A MINT. `mentl <file>:<line>` at a lambda renders
  // its row, so the row has a home; what a counted lambda carries is a name
  // nothing needed — pattern dispatch paying a wrapper to reach the arm list
  // the language already has (`Hβ.syntax.function-literal-is-an-arm-list`),
  // or a call whose params pass straight through, which is a hole. The
  // ceiling is the wheel's count and follows it DOWN: a ratchet that only
  // rises to meet a breach has stopped ratcheting, which is why the board
  // reports the counts it is inside as well as the ones it is over. 137 ->
  // 136 (2026-10-16): the parameters' minted cells left with their lambdas
  // when a parameter became its node. 136 -> 135 the same day: the walk that
  // paired each state field's name with its init left when the name became
  // its binder. 135 -> 132: the lowering's spine of capture points left when
  // a continuation was captured at any position. 132 -> 131: the forking
  // handler's step is one lambda more, and two wrappers of the specializer's
  // substitution became the holes they were.
  Bound({ceiling: 131, question: QCensus(CsEffectfulLambda)}),
  // Drift mode 10 — the seven survivors are documented sentinels, not masked
  // cases. Every wildcard that is NOT one of them is a variant the author
  // declined to enumerate, and the medium cannot tell the difference, which
  // is exactly why the bound is a count and not zero. 9 -> 7 (2026-09-28,
  // R0d): the count read 7 at pin 0bc8383e, so the bound admitted two new
  // masked cases nobody would have seen.
  Bound({ceiling: 7, question: QCensus(CsWildcardZero)}),
  // Drift mode 13 — a bug is zero or it is blocking; a masked failure is the
  // surrender-fallback Anchor 2 deletes rather than wraps.
  Bound({ceiling: 0, question: QCensus(CsFailureMask)}),
  // A print inside a `report(...)` arm corrupts WAT stdout — the wheel's own
  // emission running through the same file descriptor as its narration.
  Bound({ceiling: 0, question: QCensus(CsPrintInReport)}),
  // Drift mode 10's typed face: a wildcard arm minting `Forall`, a bare
  // `TVar`, `"Pure"` or `""` is a fabricated judgment, and a fabricated
  // judgment is indistinguishable downstream from a proven one. 20 -> 19
  // (2026-10-14, WILD): the escaping-row walk's handler-name read answered
  // `""` for an install it could not name, and left with the walk. 19 -> 17
  // (2026-10-15): the lowering's two `""` answers for an install whose
  // handler name it could not read left with the read — an install is its
  // handler's declaration. 17 -> 15 (2026-10-16): the verifier's catch-alls
  // were written as their rosters when the flow walk replaced the label
  // lattice. 15 -> 14 the same day: the callee-name read's `""` left with the
  // trailing pair a resume-bound fn took, once a nested fn captured its k.
  Bound({ceiling: 14, question: QCensus(CsWildcardFabricates)}),
  // Drift mode 10 at the arm itself (Morgan, 2026-10-13): a `_` or a bare
  // binder after other arms of a match over a sum is the roster the author
  // declined to write, and a constructor declared later joins it unread.
  // `mentl tighten` writes the roster. The ceiling is the wheel's count,
  // seen RED one below the day the shape was counted, and follows every
  // landing that lowers it; it falls to zero where the migration lands
  // (`Hβ.match.catch-all-over-a-sum-is-the-roster`). 1177 -> 1171
  // (2026-10-16): the parameter desugar and its re-sugaring render left
  // with their catch-alls when a parameter became its node. 1171 -> 1168
  // the same day: the comment gate's walks over binder names became one
  // search over the child projection, and a comment's owner reads its
  // declaration's spelling. 1168 -> 1167 the same day: the walk to a
  // position's declaration names its roster where the session's cone reads it.
  // 1167 -> 1141: the lowering's spine of capture points and the judgment's
  // continuation boundaries left when a continuation was captured at any
  // position. 1141 -> 937: `mentl tighten` wrote every catch-all of the
  // verifier and of the graph, type and effect modules it imports as its
  // roster, the day information flow became the verifier's walk. 937 -> 936
  // the same day: the callee-name read left with the resume-bound fn's
  // trailing pair.
  Bound({ceiling: 936, question: QCensus(CsWildcardOverSum)}),
  // Drift mode 15 — a value given a leading-underscore name instead of being
  // deleted. The rename silences the reader, never the fact that nothing
  // reads it.
  Bound({ceiling: 0, question: QCensus(CsUnderscoreRetain)}),
  // Drift mode 8 — an int-coded flag is an ADT the author did not write, and
  // every comparison against it is a claim the type system cannot check.
  Bound({ceiling: 0, question: QCensus(CsFlagAsInt)}),
  // Drift mode 7 — adjacent `x, x_h` parameters are one record split across
  // two positions, with position standing in for the identity the record
  // would have carried.
  Bound({ceiling: 0, question: QCensus(CsParallelArrays)}),
  // Drift mode 1 — a dispatch-slot record. The word never appears in correct
  // Mentl: the graph plus a handler IS the form a vtable approximates.
  Bound({ceiling: 0, question: QCensus(CsVtableRecord)}),
  // Drift mode 2 — scope as a parent-pointer frame stack. Env lookup is an
  // effect op; a frame walk is that op re-implemented where the handler was.
  Bound({ceiling: 0, question: QCensus(CsEnvFrame)}),
  // THE SECOND LINE ON THIS ROSTER THAT IS A REAL COUNTDOWN, and it reached
  // its endpoint on 2026-09-27 (A4). It began as the WIDE-row count: a
  // signature past eight names is a capability nobody named, and naming
  // one (`type Judging`, src/driver.mn) moved it 19 → 12 in one landing.
  // Under that sat the deeper claim — the POSITIVE row is inferred and
  // projected, and only negations, instance pins and Pure are authored —
  // and that claim is the shape now: a signature that authors ANY bare
  // positive name. `mentl tighten` wrote the residue of every such clause
  // on the wheel (1,336 clauses carried positive names; 290 were already
  // negation-only or Pure), so the wheel's signatures read as decisions:
  // `with !Mutate`, `with Pure`, `with Sample(44100)`. What survives on the
  // page is what a reader should read, and the full row is at the address
  // surface beside repr width and resume cardinality.
  //
  // The ceiling is the measured count after the sweep — the clauses the
  // verb could not rewrite (a multi-line signature head) plus the caps a
  // developer keeps on purpose — and it only falls. A new inventory refuses
  // the pin: the count is the law's gate, the prose above its residue.
  Bound({ceiling: 0, question: QCensus(CsAuthoredPositiveRow)}),
  // ─ THE ANSWERS (G2): the lines below bound questions the board could not
  // ask while it bounded shapes alone. Each was seen RED one below its
  // ceiling before it was set, and each only falls.
  //
  // The open proof obligations — every claim Verify could neither prove nor
  // refute, at its own site (`mentl query <entry> verification`). They rose
  // 37 → 39 across L-C with nothing to refuse it, five of them new in
  // src/space.mn, then 39 → 212 at TRAP, every one an index whose bound
  // claim `PInBounds` raises and the fragment cannot yet decide — debt the
  // row now states rather than a trap it hid. Falls as a claim gains its
  // proof: a precondition, a path read (#109), a refinement at a part (T1) —
  // or as a walk stops reading by index at all: the canvas's strip, its
  // tokens' neighbours, its frame roles and the field's ranking walk the
  // data they read, and the space verb's needle is a list pattern, 212 → 204.
  // Every verb's builder takes its words apart by pattern, and the help
  // catalog maps the verb table, 204 → 184 (L-F). 184 → 181 at M1's first
  // pin (2026-10-14): the query's index walks over names left with the
  // name-keyed refs. 181 → 180 (2026-10-15): a cycle's settlements read its
  // members' handles, taken once, rather than indexing the statements again.
  // 180 → 177 the same day: the unreachable facet walks the reference edges,
  // and its index walks over a name table left with the table. 177 → 174:
  // the dead voice surface's index walks left with it. 174 → 173: a written
  // row renders by a map over its terms, where an index walked them. 173 →
  // 170 (2026-10-16): the parameter builders' index reads into a list of
  // cells beside the parameters left with the list. 170 → 168 the same day:
  // the formatter's index walk over an arm's argument names left when an
  // arm's arguments became parameters.
  Bound({ceiling: 168, question: QVerifyDebt}),
  // The iteration costumes — a function that threads an incremented index
  // through its own self-call, the imperative loop in recursion's costume
  // (CLAUDE.md Anchor 6). 390 when the detector was born on 2026-07-30, 490
  // at G2, every new module still writing the shape (derive 36, space 3)
  // because nothing refused it. Falls as each family migrates to the
  // vocabulary (AU2); the detector itself is re-founded at AU1, and the
  // ceiling resets to that count then. 490 -> 489 at its birth: the
  // unconsumed-own report it was born beside became a filter. 489 -> 471 at
  // the heads landing: the canvas's walks and the space verb's argument read
  // their data by `enumerate`, `zip`, `sort` and list patterns. 471 -> 465 at
  // L-F: the address parse, the help catalog and the record renders map
  // their data, and the assembler's long division folds over its bits.
  // 465 -> 464 at Landing 1 (2026-10-13): lib/search's one left with the
  // module. 464 -> 461 at WILD (2026-10-14): the escaping-row pre-pass's
  // three index walks left with it. 461 -> 460 the same day: a data
  // segment's bytes fold into one buffer. 460 -> 450 at M1's first pin: the
  // name indexes the reference edge replaced were each an index walk — the
  // comment gate's declaration index and its span scopes, the env's
  // per-name scans, the query's name-keyed collectors. 450 -> 426
  // (2026-10-15): the dead code the facets named left with its index walks.
  // 426 -> 425 the same day: the count read 425 when a pattern became a
  // node, one under the ceiling the landings before left. 425 -> 424: the
  // formatter's renderer of a written row's terms became the type renderer's
  // map over them. 424 -> 422 (2026-10-16): the re-sugaring walk over a
  // head's parameters and the scan for unannotated ones left with the
  // parameter desugar. 422 -> 411 the same day: the comment gate's eleven
  // index walks over binders, constructors, fields and ops became one fold
  // over the child projection that answers the binder's node. 411 -> 409:
  // the formatter's and the cursor transport's scans for a line's first byte
  // became one, and the list flatten's walks one range fill. 409 -> 406: the
  // lowering's spine of capture points left when a continuation was captured
  // at any position. 406 -> 405: the ledger's per-obligation line became an
  // `each` over the debt.
  Bound({ceiling: 405, question: QCensus(CsIterationCostume)}),
  // The ghosts — cells the parser minted and the judgment never bound
  // (`mentl query <entry> ghosts`): names, parameters, predicates and
  // annotations that are not yet cells inference writes, which is why `refs
  // of` misses a type annotation and a claim sits at the application rather
  // than at its value. It never rises: new code mints ghosts at the rate it
  // writes names, so a landing that adds code binds a class of them in the
  // same landing — the bound is how positions become cells (#108), one class
  // at a time. Its comment once told each landing to raise it, and four
  // landings did (18,681 → 19,734). The first class paid: an unannotated
  // parameter's parser cell is bound to the parameter's own cell
  // (`build_param_types`), 19,747 → 10,604. The second: an absent return
  // annotation is no node of its own, where a unit literal was indexed at
  // every unannotated function's name, 10,665 → 6,089. The third,
  // 6,092 → 477 when the verbs integration's line fixes rose it by three: a
  // declaration's node is bound where the judgment registers it — a variant
  // to its constructor, an op to its operation, a handler to its type, any
  // other declaration to unit (`bind_declared`) — a statement in a block
  // carries its expression's value as a let does, and a desugared parameter
  // is ONE cell (the lambda head's cover node, or the one handle that also
  // names it) where a second was minted beside it. The fourth, 492 → 150 when
  // the canvas's holes rose it by thirteen: a `??` is one cell whose id is its
  // own handle (`nhole`), where a second cell was minted for the id alone,
  // and a destructuring let's statement cell is the match it becomes
  // (`desugar_block`). The fifth, 154 → 112 at L-F: a match's arms meet in a
  // result cell the judgment mints and the match node reads it, as an if's
  // node reads its branches, where every arm had been unified into the node
  // itself and left it the class's root; and a nominal record literal's head
  // is the type it names. Next are the return and parameter annotations and
  // refinement predicates; one of the return annotations' left at WILD
  // (2026-10-14) with the escaping-row walk's name-list concat, 112 -> 111;
  // 111 -> 91 (2026-10-15) with the dead code the facets named; 91 -> 86 the
  // same day with the return annotations of the five record accessors the
  // install stack's entry type replaced. 86 -> 0 the same day: an authored
  // return or let annotation is bound to the type it declares, a function
  // type's implicit row tail stands at no position, and a refinement's
  // predicate is judged as the expression it is.
  Bound({ceiling: 0, question: QGhosts}),
  // Dead code: a function of the wheel's own layer the entry cannot reach
  // over the reference edges (`mentl query src/main.mn unreachable`). It
  // read zero when the facet first walked the edges and one a landing later
  // (2026-10-15, a callee reader in src/lower.mn), since nothing bounded it; a
  // function the wheel stops calling leaves in the landing that stops
  // calling it.
  Bound({ceiling: 0, question: QUnreachable}),
  // Speculation is a choice whose resumptions the trail brackets: a
  // checkpoint is pushed by the graph handler's own arm and by the arms of
  // the two forking handlers that answer `choose`, and by nothing else. A
  // function that pushes one has bracketed a speculation by hand — the
  // bracket the forking handlers hold once. Seen RED at 8 the day the five
  // hand brackets became performs of `choose` (2026-10-16).
  Bound({ceiling: 3, question: QRefsOf("graph_push_checkpoint")}),
  // ─ PROSE BY CLASS (SA-5, MOD-13). A comment is graph content, so what
  // SYNTAX §Comments says a comment is not is a census, never a review
  // finding. Each class falls as the module carrying it is touched; F strips
  // the decoration and AU2 rewrites the coordinates into declaration names.
  //
  // Module coordinates — a file and a line where the declaration's name was
  // the edge; each rots at the first edit above it. 29 where a substring
  // read of the extension and colon answered 34: five of those were the
  // extension in prose with no line after it. 27 -> 23 (2026-10-14, WILD):
  // the dead narrowing walk's header cited four. 23 -> 17 (2026-10-15): the
  // headers of the dead voice, eight-loop and proposer chain, and the
  // composition tallies trued with the modules they described. 17 -> 15
  // (2026-10-15): the session's and the pipeline's notes over the walk the
  // link node replaced.
  Bound({ceiling: 15, question: QCensus(CsProseClass(PcCoordinate))}),
  // Repository paths that name no file: a comment citing a path the tree
  // does not hold.
  Bound({ceiling: 1, question: QCensus(CsProseClass(PcPathNoFile))}),
  // Hex commit tokens — history belongs to git, never on the node. 44 -> 43
  // (2026-10-16): a note on the label lattice left with the lattice.
  Bound({ceiling: 43, question: QCensus(CsProseClass(PcCommit))}),
  // Numbered citations of the archived spec corpus. 20 -> 19 (2026-10-15):
  // the banner over the pattern type left when a pattern became a node.
  Bound({ceiling: 19, question: QCensus(CsProseClass(PcSpecCitation))}),
  // Lifecycle prose — what was, where SYNTAX asks for what is. 39 -> 38
  // (2026-10-15): the note over the sugar's callees that dated when the
  // free-name walk began drawing them left with the by-spelling rows.
  Bound({ceiling: 38, question: QCensus(CsProseClass(PcLifecycle))}),
  // Archaeology — the seed era's vocabulary and its design notes. 68 -> 67
  // (2026-10-15): the note over the type annotation's node kind that said
  // why its tag stood last. 67 -> 66 (2026-10-15): a stale note over the
  // stdin route left. 66 -> 65 (2026-10-16): the session's note over its
  // module-grain re-derivation left with it. 65 -> 63 the same day: the
  // notes on the label lattice left with the lattice.
  Bound({ceiling: 63, question: QCensus(CsProseClass(PcArchaeology))}),
  // Decoration runs; the formatter's decoration strip takes this to zero
  // (PLAN §11, the project canonical). 267 -> 266 (2026-10-15): the pattern
  // type's banner left when a pattern became a node. 266 -> 265
  // (2026-10-16): the parameter re-sugar's banner left with the re-sugar.
  // 265 -> 255 the same day: the verifier's section banners left when its
  // comments were trued with the flow walk. 255 -> 254: the segment walk's
  // banner left when the ??-fan became one choice.
  Bound({ceiling: 254, question: QCensus(CsProseClass(PcBanner))}),
  // A COMMENT NEVER SILENCES A GATE (SYNTAX §Comments). Each marker mutes a
  // text row of tools/drift-patterns.tsv that a structural census reads
  // correctly — a string literal is text, a one-shot concat is not an
  // accumulator — and each falls as its row becomes a shape. At zero the
  // marker's grammar deletes from drift-audit.sh. 134 -> 132 at the heads
  // landing; 132 -> 131 at L-F, the marker over the nominal record head's
  // name read leaving with the read; 131 -> 129 at WILD (2026-10-14), the
  // two inside the escaping-row walk leaving with the walk; 129 -> 128 at
  // M1's first pin, the env's scope-mark marker leaving with the rewrite;
  // 128 -> 124 (2026-10-15), four over dead code leaving with it; 124 -> 121
  // the same day, the two over the install's name sentinel leaving with the
  // name read and a resume-bound call's pair of markers becoming one. 121 ->
  // 115 (2026-10-16): the count read 117 at the pin before, and the two over
  // the free-name walk's unions left when each union became one flat list.
  // 115 -> 113 the same day: the two over a resume-bound call's trailing
  // pair and its callee-name read left when a nested fn captured its k.
  Bound({ceiling: 113, question: QCensus(CsProseClass(PcSilencer))})
]

// The board: every bound answered by the medium's own answer to its question.
//
// The answer is what `ask` returns — the same projection `mentl query` renders,
// not a number recovered from its rendering. That distinction is the landing
// the board was born in: the old path ran a walk, printed "N site(s)", and
// then asked a regex what N was, so a change to the SENTENCE could break the
// GATE. Nothing here can drift from the answer, because there is nothing
// between them; and a question the board can ask is any question the query
// grammar can, not only a census shape.
fn board_read() with !Mutate = board_bounds() |> map(bound_standing)

fn bound_standing(b) with !Mutate = match b {
  Bound(r) => (b, standing_of(r.ceiling, located_answer(ask(r.question)))),
}

fn standing_of(ceiling, answer) = match answer {
  Some(found) => match found {
    (label, sites) => if len(sites) > ceiling { Over(label, sites) } else { Within(label, sites) },
  },
  None => Unlocated("a question answered without sites — it cannot be bounded by count"),
}

// One line, in the medium's voice: the question's label, what it found, and
// — when the bound is breached — the fact that a count rose rather than a
// rule fired, which is the honest description of what a ratchet knows.
fn board_line(entry) = match entry {
  (b, standing) => match b {
    Bound(r) => match standing {
      Within(label, sites) => "  · {int_to_str(len(sites))} {label} — within {int_to_str(r.ceiling)}\n",
      // A breach names WHERE, because the number alone is the one thing the
      // developer cannot act on. The sites come from the same answer that
      // decided the breach — one read, no second question.
      Over(label, sites) => "  ✗ {int_to_str(len(sites))} {label} — ROSE past {int_to_str(r.ceiling)}\n{board_sites(sites)}",
      Unlocated(why) => "  ✗ a bound over {why}\n",
    },
  },
}

// The sites a breach names, the first fifty of them: a line over the ghosts
// can carry twenty thousand, and the rest are one question away.
fn board_sites(sites) = {
  let shown = sites |> take(50) |> map(board_site_line) |> str_concat_all
  if len(sites) > 50 {
    "{shown}      … {int_to_str(len(sites) - 50)} more — the full list is the question's own answer under `mentl query`\n"
  } else {
    shown
  }
}

fn board_site_line(site) = match site {
  (module, span) => "      {module}:{show_span(span)}\n",
}

fn board_breached(entry) with Pure = match entry {
  (_b, standing) => match standing {
    Within(_, _) => false,
    Over(_, _) => true,
    Unlocated(_) => true,
  },
}
